The '''Estadi de Balboa''' is the national stadium of [[Balboa]], located in the [[Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station|Portal de Sant Cristòfor]] district of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]]. With a capacity of 80,402, it is the largest stadium in the country and the principal venue for major football matches, cup finals, and international events. The stadium is not the home ground of any football club; it is used for national team matches, domestic cup finals, and continental competition fixtures.

The stadium was completed on 1 April 2007 as part of the broader Sant Cristòfor high-speed rail construction project, which also included the reconstruction of the adjacent [[Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station|Portal de Sant Cristòfor]] railway station. The co-development of the stadium and station was designed to provide direct high-speed rail access to the venue for event crowds, with HSR services making a special stop at Portal de Sant Cristòfor during events.

== History ==

=== Planning and construction ===

The Estadi de Balboa was conceived as part of the Sant Cristòfor high-speed rail project, which began construction in 2004. The project included the construction of the [[Sant Cristòfor–Areza HSR line|Sant Cristòfor–Areza high-speed rail line]] and associated infrastructure, including the rebuilding of stations along the shared trunk section between the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] and [[Varakí TDV (CristoCarril)|Varakí TDV]]. The Portal de Sant Cristòfor station, located approximately 3 km south of the Central Terminal, was selected as the site for the national stadium complex, taking advantage of the HSR alignment to provide rapid crowd distribution.

Construction of the stadium and the rebuilt station was carried out simultaneously, with both completed on 1 April 2007. The stadium opened one year before the HSR line began commercial service in 2008, and two years before the [[Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line|Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line]] opened in 2009.

=== Opening and early years ===

The stadium opened on 1 April 2007 with a friendly match between the [[Balboa national football team]] and a selected AFA all-star squad. The inaugural match drew a capacity crowd of 80,402, establishing the venue as the premier sporting facility in the country.

Since its opening, the Estadi de Balboa has served as the primary venue for the [[Balboa national football team|national team]]'s home matches, hosting World Cup qualifiers, international friendlies, and continental competition fixtures. The stadium is also the traditional venue for domestic cup finals.

== Events ==

=== Domestic football ===

The Estadi de Balboa hosts the finals of both major Balboan domestic cup competitions:

* The '''[[Copa de l'Istme]]''', the primary cup competition open to all clubs in the four national tiers, holds its final at the Estadi de Balboa. The single-elimination tournament culminates in a showpiece final at the national stadium.
* The '''[[Copa Balboa]]''', the secondary cup competition open to LFB2 clubs and below, also holds its final at the Estadi de Balboa.

The stadium also hosts the '''Gran Final''' of [[La Lliga de l'Istme|La Lliga]], the match between the Apertura and Clausura champions that determines the overall league champion.

