The stadium's selection as a recurring host for the Abyalan Champions' Cup final reflects its status as one of the premier football venues in the Abyalan region, with modern facilities and direct high-speed rail access for travelling supporters.

=== Other events ===

In addition to football, the Estadi de Balboa has hosted concerts, athletics events, and national celebrations. The stadium's location adjacent to the Portal de Sant Cristòfor station provides direct rail access from across the country, making it a practical venue for large-scale events that draw crowds from beyond Sant Cristòfor.

== Transportation ==

The Estadi de Balboa is directly served by the [[Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station|Portal de Sant Cristòfor]] railway station, located adjacent to the stadium complex. The station is served by [[CristoCarril]] [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]] and [[Line C (CristoCarril)|Line C]] commuter rail services under regular operation.

During events at the stadium, the station is additionally served by high-speed rail services on the [[Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line|Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line]], which makes a special stop at Portal de Sant Cristòfor to provide direct high-speed connections from the Central Terminal and from [[Varakí TDV (CristoCarril)|Varakí TDV]]. This event service adds approximately 2 minutes to the end-to-end HSR journey time and is scheduled around the event timetable, with increased service frequency before and after events to manage crowd movements.

The station is also served by [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Metro]] Lines 2 and 4, which provide connections across the [[Original (ciutat)|Original]] district and to neighbouring ciutats including [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]], [[Sant Martí (Sant Cristòfor)|Sant Martí]], and [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]]. The [[Tramvia de Sant Cristòfor|tram]] network provides additional local transport options within Sant Cristòfor.

